  "slug": "immrep25-unseen-peptides-fb4c",
  "summary": "IMMREP25 and new structure-informed models expose limited generalization of TCR specificity prediction to peptides absent from training data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is generalization of TCR:pMHC prediction to peptides absent from training data. IMMREP25 results show the strongest methods, including structural modeling approaches, reaching macro-AUC of about 0.60 on unseen peptides, a modest level. StriMap pairs structure-informed deep learning with TCR-peptide-HLA prediction and applies it to screening bacterial peptides to identify AS-linked molecular features. Alongside this, an IEDB audit finds 55.8% of MHC-I immunopeptidomics data computationally labeled, producing recursive bias; deepMHCflare reframes epitope discovery as learning-to-rank. The new emphasis is evaluation validity and label provenance alongside architecture. ViraHinter and the DefensePredictor and genomic language-model studies apply related sequence and embedding methods to virus-host and prokaryotic defense proteins, but do not address TCR specificity directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-06"
}
